## Task board

Tasks live in `roadmap/tasks/{open,doing,done}/` per the org-wide file-based
kanban system; `roadmap/tasks/TASKS.md` holds the conventions. Read it before
picking up, creating or updating a task.

| ID | Title | Priority | Depends on |
|---|---|---|---|
| 001 | Resolve scanner role from phone number at login | high | — |
| 002 | Protect `/qr` and `/geo` with a secret token | high | — |
| 003 | Split the scan-result page by role, real counts | high | 001 |
| 004 | Confirmation guard against accidental rescans | medium | — |
| 005 | Wire up the `photo` and `photocover` projections | high | — |
| 006 | Show the cover photo + confirm identity before registering | high | 005 |
| 007 | Migrate `superfluids`/`tablerow` → `jrgensen/stream` + `cqrs` | medium | — |

The decided-but-unimplemented behaviours described above are tracked there. When
you implement one, work the task file as you go rather than retro-filling it, and
update the *Known deviations* list here once the deviation is actually gone.

PRD folders (`roadmap/prd/{draft,doing,done}/`) do not exist yet — create them via
the `prd` skill if a change needs a spec first.

